<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rigsråd</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">to 1660</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Danish Council of the Realm</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rigsråd, or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rigsradet">Council of the Realm</a>, was the council of the Danish high nobility and, until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a>, which shared power with the king from the later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>. Each new king signed an accession charter guaranteeing its privileges. It was abolished when Frederick III introduced absolute monarchy in 1660.</p></div>
